{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"CRM"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Industry Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should be able to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Explain major biochemical mechanisms"},{"text":"Understand human physiology"},{"text":"Explain major drug classes"},{"text":"Understand pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics"},{"text":"Explain basic mechanisms of action"},{"text":"Understand major disease areas"},{"text":"Understand drug-development stages"},{"text":"Read pharmaceutical product information critically"},{"text":"Communicate scientific information clearly"},{"text":"Perform basic market research"},{"text":"Analyze competitor products"},{"text":"Prepare product presentations"},{"text":"Understand pharmaceutical sales workflows"},{"text":"Understand pharmacovigilance fundamentals"},{"text":"Understand GMP/GCP concepts"},{"text":"Use Excel confidently"},{"text":"Build basic Power BI dashboards"},{"text":"Understand CRM workflows"},{"text":"Complete a pharmaceutical-industry internship"},{"text":"Choose a clear commercial or technical specialization"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"For a Pharma Executive career, the student should not rely solely on biochemistry."},{"type":"p","text":"A stronger positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Biochemistry","Pharmacology","Pharmaceutical Product Knowledge","Medical Communication","Sales/Marketing","Market Analytics","Regulatory Awareness","Industry Internship"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"If the student prefers a commercial career, an MBA or specialized postgraduate program can accelerate progression into product management, marketing and business development. If the student prefers a scientific career, M.Sc Biochemistry/Biotechnology or a relevant specialized PG route is more appropriate."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Career Pathways"},{"type":"tab